        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ui): turn large pasted text into compact composer attachments",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users pasting large plain-text blocks into the Control UI chat composer would dump the entire block into the textarea, making the composer hard to scan and easy to send accidentally.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis change treats plain-text paste payloads over 2000 characters as existing composer attachments with `text/plain` file payloads instead of introducing a separate composer-only state model. That keeps send, queue, retry, payload snapshotting, removal, and cleanup on the existing attachment path; the compact preview adds a “show in composer” action for users who want to edit the pasted text inline.\n\nNormal short text paste behavior is unchanged, and the existing data-URL/image paste path is checked before large text handling so image paste behavior continues to use the current attachment flow.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can paste large text into chat without the textarea becoming unwieldy. The pasted text appears as a compact block, can be removed, can be expanded back into the composer, and is still included in the submitted chat payload when left as a block.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD`\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs ui/src/pages/chat/chat-view.test.ts ui/src/pages/chat/chat-send.test.ts` (`203` tests passed)\n- Browser smoke on `pnpm dev:ui:mock -- --host 127.0.0.1 --port 5199`:\n  - pasted >2000 characters and verified a compact pasted-text block appeared while the textarea stayed empty\n  - removed the pasted-text block\n  - pasted again and used “show in composer”; verified the full text returned to the textarea and the block was removed\n- Send payload preservation is covered by the focused `handleSendChat` regression test for `text/plain` pasted-text attachments.\n",
        "branch": "brzezowski/composer-large-paste-block",
